[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m The "stars and bars" theorem states that the number of ways to distribute \( n \) indistinguishable objects into \( k \) distinguishable bins is given by the binomial coefficient:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \binom{n+k-1}{k-1}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
