[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m In this problem:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m - \( n = 4 \) (the number of indistinguishable balls)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m - \( k = 2 \) (the number of distinguishable boxes)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m We need to calculate:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \binom{4+2-1}{2-1} = \binom{5}{1}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m The binomial coefficient \(\binom{5}{1}\) is calculated as follows:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \binom{5}{1} = \frac{5!}{1!(5-1)!} = \frac{5!}{1! \cdot 4!} = \frac{5 \cdot 4!}{1 \cdot 4!} = 5
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Thus, the number of ways to put 4 indistinguishable balls into 2 distinguishable boxes is:
