[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Taking the square root of both sides, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m s = \sqrt{49} = 7 \text{ inches}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Next, we consider the folding of the square. When the square is folded so that one pair of opposite corners coincide, the fold line is the diagonal of the square. This diagonal divides the square into two congruent right triangles. Each triangle has legs that are equal to the side length of the square, and the hypotenuse is the diagonal of the square.
