[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m A square piece of paper is folded once so that one pair of opposite corners coincide. When the paper is unfolded, two congruent triangles have been formed. Given that the area of the original square is $49$ square inches, what is the number of inches in the perimeter of one of these triangles? Express your answer in simplest radical form. Let's think step by step and output the final answer within \boxed{}.
