[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m s = \sqrt{49} = 7 \text{ inches}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m When the square is folded so that one pair of opposite corners coincide, a diagonal is formed, dividing the square into two congruent right triangles. Each triangle has legs that are equal to the side length of the square, and the hypotenuse is the diagonal of the square.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m The length of the diagonal \(d\) of a square with side length \(s\) can be calculated using the Pythagorean theorem:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
