[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m The total number of ways to choose 3 marbles out of 11 is given by the combination formula \(C(n, k) = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\), where \(n\) is the total number of items, \(k\) is the number of items to choose, and \(!\) denotes factorial. So, the total number of ways to choose 3 marbles out of 11 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[C(11, 3) = \frac{11!}{3!(11-3)!} = \frac{11 \times 10 \times 9}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 165\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Next, we calculate the number of ways she can choose 3 marbles that include both the green and the purple ones. If both green and purple are chosen, then she only needs to choose 1 more marble from the remaining 9 (since there are 11 marbles in total and 2 are already chosen). The number of ways to do this is:
