[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m [response] To solve this problem, we first determine the probability of winning in a single turn. The probability of rolling a 1 or a 6 on a standard die is \(\frac{2}{6} = \frac{1}{3}\), and the probability of the coin showing heads is \(\frac{1}{2}\). Therefore, the probability of winning in one turn is \(\frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{2} = \frac{1}{6}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m The probability of not winning in a single turn is \(1 - \frac{1}{6} = \frac{5}{6}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
