[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Since the GCD of \(m\) and \(n\) is 8, both \(m\) and \(n\) can be expressed as multiples of 8, say \(m = 8a\) and \(n = 8b\), where \(a\) and \(b\) are coprime (i.e., \(\text{GCD}(a, b) = 1\)). Substituting these into the equation gives \(8a \times 8b = 896\), or \(a \times b = 14\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
