[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m [response] To find the radius of the circle inscribed in a triangle (inradius), we can use the formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ r = \frac{A}{s} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m where \(A\) is the area of the triangle and \(s\) is the semi-perimeter of the triangle.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m First, calculate the semi-perimeter \(s\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ s = \frac{AB + AC + BC}{2} = \frac{12 + 14 + 16}{2} = 21 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Next, use Heron's formula to find the area \(A\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ A = \sqrt{s(s-AB)(s-AC)(s-BC)} = \sqrt{21(21-12)(21-14)(21-16)} = \sqrt{21 \times 9 \times 7 \times 5} = \sqrt{6615} = 21\sqrt{15} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Finally, calculate the inradius \(r\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ r = \frac{A}{s} = \frac{21\sqrt{15}}{21} = \sqrt{15} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
