[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m [response] To calculate the interest earned on a deposit compounded annually, we use the formula for compound interest:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ A = P \left(1 + \frac{r}{n}\right)^{nt} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m where:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m - \(A\) is the amount of money accumulated after n years, including interest.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m - \(P\) is the principal amount (the initial amount of money).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m - \(r\) is the annual interest rate (decimal).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m - \(n\) is the number of times that interest is compounded per year.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m - \(t\) is the time the money is invested for in years.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Given:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m - \(P = 10,000\)
