[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m [response] To solve this problem, we need to calculate the probability of winning the game before the fourth turn. The game is won if a die shows a 1 or a 6 (which has a probability of \( \frac{2}{6} = \frac{1}{3} \)) and a coin shows heads (which has a probability of \( \frac{1}{2} \)). Therefore, the probability of winning in a single turn is \( \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{2} = \frac{1}{6} \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m The probability of not winning in a single turn is \( 1 - \frac{1}{6} = \frac{5}{6} \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m The probability of winning before the fourth turn is the sum of the probabilities of winning on the first, second, or third turn:
