[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m [response] To find the radius of the circle inscribed in triangle \(ABC\) with sides \(AB = 12\), \(AC = 14\), and \(BC = 16\), we can use the formula for the radius \(r\) of the inscribed circle, which is given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ r = \frac{A}{s} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m where \(A\) is the area of the triangle and \(s\) is the semi-perimeter of the triangle.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m First, calculate the semi-perimeter \(s\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ s = \frac{12 + 14 + 16}{2} = 21 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Next, use Heron's formula to find the area \(A\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ A = \sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ A = \sqrt{21(21-12)(21-14)(21-16)} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ A = \sqrt{21 \times 9 \times 7 \times 5} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ A = \sqrt{6615} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ A = 21\sqrt{15} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Now, substitute \(A\) and \(s\) into the formula for \(r\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ r = \frac{21\sqrt{15}}{21} = \sqrt{15} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Thus, the radius of the inscribed circle is \(\boxed{\sqrt{15}}\).
