[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w} = \|\mathbf{v}\| \|\mathbf{w}\| \cos \theta
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m where \(\theta\) is the angle between the vectors. Given \(\|\mathbf{v}\| = 3\) and \(\|\mathbf{w}\| = 4\), the expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w} = 3 \cdot 4 \cdot \cos \theta = 12 \cos \theta
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m The minimum value of \(\cos \theta\) is \(-1\), which occurs when the vectors are in opposite directions. Therefore, the minimum value of the dot product is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 12 \cdot (-1) = -12
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Thus, the minimum value of \(\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w}\) is \(\boxed{-12}\).
