[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m The mean of these three integers is \(n\). According to the problem, the product divided by the mean is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \frac{(n-1)n(n+1)}{n} = 24
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m (n-1)(n+1) = 24
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Solving this equation, we find:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m n^2 - 1 = 24 \implies n^2 = 25 \implies n = 5
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Thus, the largest of the three consecutive integers is \(\boxed{6}\).
