[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m [response] Given the polynomial \( p(x) = x^2 + ax + b \) with roots \( 2a \) and \( b \), we can use Vieta's formulas, which relate the coefficients of the polynomial to sums and products of its roots. According to Vieta's formulas, for the polynomial \( x^2 + ax + b \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 1. The sum of the roots is equal to the negation of the coefficient of \( x \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m    \[
