[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m A standard die has 6 faces, and a fair coin has 2 sides. The probability of rolling a 1 or a 6 on the die is \(\frac{2}{6} = \frac{1}{3}\), and the probability of the coin showing heads is \(\frac{1}{2}\). Therefore, the probability of winning on a single turn is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{2} = \frac{1}{6}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m The probability of losing on a single turn is:
