[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m [response] Given the polynomial \( p(x) = x^2 + ax + b \) with roots \( 2a \) and \( b \), we can use Vieta's formulas. According to Vieta's formulas, the sum of the roots is equal to the negation of the coefficient of \( x \), and the product of the roots is equal to the constant term. Therefore, we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 2a + b = -a
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 2a \cdot b = b
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m From the second equation, we can factor out \( b \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m b(2a - 1) = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m This gives us two cases: \( b = 0 \) or \( 2a - 1 = 0 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m **Case 1:** \( b = 0 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Substituting \( b = 0 \) into the first equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 2a = -a \implies 3a = 0 \implies a = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m But this would make the roots \( 0 \) and \( 0 \), which contradicts the condition that the roots are distinct. So, \( b \neq 0 \).
