[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we first analyze the given inequalities involving the function \( f(x) = x^2 + 6x + 1 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m The inequalities are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 1. \( f(x) + f(y) \le 0 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 2. \( f(x) - f(y) \le 0 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m Starting with the first inequality:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ f(x) + f(y) = x^2 + 6x + 1 + y^2 + 6y + 1 = x^2 + y^2 + 6x + 6y + 2 \le 0 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m This can be rewritten as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[ (x+3)^2 + (y+3)^2 \le 16 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m which represents a circle centered at \((-3, -3)\) with radius 4.
