[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 1. The sum of the roots is equal to the negation of the coefficient of \( x \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m    2a + b = -a \implies 3a + b = 0 \implies b = -3a
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 2. The product of the roots is equal to the constant term:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m    (2a)(b) = b \implies 2ab = b
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m    Since \( b \neq 0 \) (the roots are distinct), we can divide both sides by \( b \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m    2a = 1 \implies a = \frac{1}{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m    \]
