[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m When the square is folded so that one pair of opposite corners coincide, a diagonal is formed, dividing the square into two congruent right triangles. Each triangle has legs of length \(7\) inches and a hypotenuse equal to the diagonal of the square.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m The length of the diagonal \(d\) of the square can be calculated using the Pythagorean theorem:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2111625)[0m \[
